{ amse_premod_immed_high.init - a DSEE derived object of be_com/backend.ins.pas (cc.a88k
  only): the initializer of the section amse_premod_immed_high (0x2B6D40: 8
  longwords, the highest displacement a premodifying load or store takes, by instr_attr_t's amse).  Included by tm_utils.pas.

  No Apollo copy survives; reconstructed from the DOMAIN C 6.9 binary
  cc.a88k, the section's bytes.

  How the section is shared (docs/questions.md 161, settled by
  translator PB2): backend.ins.pas declares the section's variable for
  every unit (`var (amse_premod_immed_high) amse_premod_immed_high: ...'); this file, included by
  the one unit that holds the data, gives it its initial value with a
  `define' statement (the language reference's section 7.2.2, method 2).
  dpc lays the defined variable out in the named section with its data.

  Not known from the original: the file's layout. }

define amse_premod_immed_high := [
    0, 15, 32767, 15, 127, 127, 15, 0];
